  data: {
    LLM: "MÃ©morise by position! Instead of trying to remember '7, King, Ace, 4', remember 'Left 7, Middle-Left King, etc.'. Most players forget their cards within the first 3 minutes. If you are targeted, watch the other player's eyesâ€”if they hesitated for even a second before 'Giving' the penalty, they likely don't remember their hand and are just trying to get rid of a card. Accuse them immediately!\n\nThe 'Sacrifice' Bluff: If you hold a 6, and a 9 is revealed in the pyramid, you can 'Give' the penalty pretending you have the 9. If the other player is a coward and accepts, you won! If they call your bluff, you take the penalty, but you've established a 'Dangerous' persona that might make them more hesitant to challenge your REAL cards later in the game.\n\nSocial Engineering (Targeting): Don't target the same person every time. Spread the penalties around based on who is winning (remembering the most). If you see someone has successfully proven their cards twice, they are 'Hot'. Never 'Deny' their claims. Target the players who have been 'Double-Penalized' alreadyâ€”they are likely flustered and more likely to accept a bluff.",
    Player: "MÃ©morise by position! Instead of trying to remember '7, King, Ace, 4', remember 'Left 7, Middle-Left King, etc.'. Most players forget their cards within the first 3 minutes. If you are targeted, watch the other player's eyesâ€”if they hesitated for even a second before 'Giving' the penalty, they likely don't remember their hand and are just trying to get rid of a card. Accuse them immediately!\n\nThe 'Sacrifice' Bluff: If you hold a 6, and a 9 is revealed in the pyramid, you can 'Give' the penalty pretending you have the 9. If the other player is a coward and accepts, you won! If they call your bluff, you take the penalty, but you've established a 'Dangerous' persona that might make them more hesitant to challenge your REAL cards later in the game.\n\nSocial Engineering (Targeting): Don't target the same person every time. Spread the penalties around based on who is winning (remembering the most). If you see someone has successfully proven their cards twice, they are 'Hot'. Never 'Deny' their claims. Target the players who have been 'Double-Penalized' alreadyâ€”they are likely flustered and more likely to accept a bluff.",
